# Contributing and CI

Canonical **human** documentation for commits, `[TEST COMMIT]`, pull requests, local testing, and docs PRs: `CONTRIBUTING.md`. Prefer that file over restating rules here when advising contributors.

## New source files

Per `CONTRIBUTING.md`, every new code file must start with:

```cpp
/*
 * SWC-DB© Copyright since 2019 Alex Kashirin <kashirin.alex@gmail.com>
 * License details at <https://github.com/kashirin-alex/swc-db/#license>
 */
```

CMake files use `#` comment form of the same notice. Contributions grant rights under project copyright; see `CONTRIBUTING.md` before submitting.

## Style enforcement

- No `.clang-format` / `.editorconfig` — match neighboring code
- Compiler: `-Wall -Werror` (and C++ `-Wextra -Wpedantic`) via `cmake/FlagsWarnings.cmake`

## CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`)

- `gate` job runs on every push/PR; main matrix runs only if the **head** commit message contains `[TEST COMMIT]` (PR head SHA or push tip — not `github.event.head_commit`, which is null on `pull_request`)
- Matrix: `ubuntu-24.04`, g++-12/13/14 and clang++-16/17/18, `O_LEVEL`, `SWC_IMPL_SOURCE` ON/OFF; default `THRIFT: ['0.20.0']`, `TEST: [1]`
- Sparse `include`: `TEST=2` integration on g++-13 unit-test O_LEVEL/IMPL pairs; one `THRIFT=0.23.0` build
- Default CI configure uses `-DSWC_LANGUAGES=NONE`; install prefix `/opt/swcdb`

Do not assume CI ran on every push; include `[TEST COMMIT]` on the head commit when intentionally triggering the workflow. See also `docs/build/test/` and `evals/QUALITY_EVALUATION_REPORT.md`.
